From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 22:41:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Let the embedder drive text input values and selection
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DocumentMutator::set_text_input_value pushes the JS-side IDL .value into
the text editor and records it as TextInputData.value_override. Layout
construction re-derives the display text from the value attribute on
every pass; the override takes precedence so a JS value write isn't
clobbered back to the attribute text on the next frame. While the
override is set, attribute writes/removals no longer touch the editor
(they only change defaultValue per HTML's decoupling).

Maps HTML selectionStart/selectionEnd (UTF-16 code units) onto the
parley editor's byte-offset selection so the existing focused-node
caret/selection paint renders what the embedder's Selection API state
describes.

set_text_input_value bailed with false when the element had no
text-input data yet: which is every .value write landing between parse
and the first layout pass (create_text_editor only runs at construct).
Scripts that assign input/textarea values at parse time painted nothing
until the next IDL write forced a repaint. Seed an editor for
text-bearing elements (textarea, text-ish inputs) and let construct's
update branch pick the override up on first layout.

Co-authored-by: Luís Duarte <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
